      "side": 1,
      "message": "What\u0027s the maximum number of atoms, 3 or 4?  If it\u0027s 4, does the logic work too?",
      "revId": "61326371d90adfc1a2193bae56af2b09450af6be",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "819aa808_25087306",
        "filename": "kernel/trace/trace_events_hist.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1621,
      "author": {
        "id": 1499410
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-08-30T23:51:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Currently there is a maximum depth in the parse tree of 3 (root node being 0). So if it is completely balanced tree there can be up to 7 operators in the expression. I need to change to to be more inline with the previous behavior which allowed a max of 4 operators.\n\nFor expressions with greater than 2 operators we need some additional logic to handle the associativity.\n\ne.g. 4*3/2*2 would currently be evaluated as (4*3)/(2*2) \u003d\u003d 3 instead of ((4*3)/2)*2 \u003d\u003d 12.\n\nThanks for pointing those out, will update in the next patchset.",
      "parentUuid": "2fd97643_8a791e63",
      "revId": "61326371d90adfc1a2193bae56af2b09450af6be",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "afa1c233_8f4cf30e",
        "filename": "kernel/trace/trace_events_hist.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1621,
      "author": {
        "id": 1499410
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-01T20:40:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maximum number of sub-expression restored to 3. The shape of the parse tree has no effect on this as was the behavior before.\n\nFixed the associativity issue. Operators of same precedence are always evaluated left to right.",
      "parentUuid": "819aa808_25087306",
      "revId": "61326371d90adfc1a2193bae56af2b09450af6be",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ac1e69fd_ab614da2",
        "filename": "kernel/trace/trace_events_hist.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1631,
      "author": {
        "id": 1613258
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-08-27T21:03:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m afraid this logic won\u0027t work correctly because it now searches the string backward.  If the expression has sym-offset, it\u0027ll find the \u0027-\u0027 in the \"sym-offset\" always.  Then it won\u0027t detect the operator like in \"$x - field.sym-offset\", no?",
      "revId": "61326371d90adfc1a2193bae56af2b09450af6be",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d5d1b219_3f237bff",
        "filename": "kernel/trace/trace_events_hist.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1631,
      "author": {
        "id": 1499410
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-08-30T23:51:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is that a valid use case? IIUC the sym-offset is for printing keys as symbol+offset. When applied to a variable in an expression it has no effect and evaluates to the same as the variable.\n\ne.g \nkmem/rss_stat $ echo \u0027hist:keys\u003dcommon_pid:vals\u003dsize.sym-offset,size\u0027 \u003e\u003e trigger\n\nkmem/rss_stat $ cat hist\n\n# event histogram\n#\n# trigger info: hist:keys\u003dcommon_pid:vals\u003dhitcount,size.sym-offset,size:sort\u003dhitcount:size\u003d2048 [active]\n#\n\n{ common_pid:       1957 } hitcount:          1  size:     524288  size:     524288\n{ common_pid:       2364 } hitcount:         11  size:   17567744  size:   17567744\n\nThe old logic also bails out with FIELD_OP_NONE as soon as it finds sym-offset. (though it is scanning form left to right). I think this is consistent with that.\n\ne.g. old logic will bail out on \"field.sym-offset-$x\" without checking the subtraction operator.",
      "parentUuid": "ac1e69fd_ab614da2",
      "revId": "61326371d90adfc1a2193bae56af2b09450af6be",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "787761b3_7f678370",
        "filename": "kernel/trace/trace_events_hist.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1631,
